WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.608
The day after Tom and Huck's adventure in the tavern, Becky reminded everyone that she was having a picnic.

2
00:00:05.609 --> 00:00:08.030
This interrupted Tom's thoughts.

3
00:00:08.031 --> 00:00:12.062
He stopped dreaming of Injun Joe, and he stopped dreaming of gold.

4
00:00:12.063 --> 00:00:15.896
The only thing he could think about was Becky and the picnic.

5
00:00:15.897 --> 00:00:21.953
That night Tom couldn't sleep. He stayed up, waiting for Huck to call.

6
00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:27.975
But Huck didn't call, so the next morning a sleepy Tom joined the rest of the children at the ferry landing.

7
00:00:27.976 --> 00:00:34.458
As they were getting ready to board the ferry, Tom overheard Becky's mother tell her, "You'll be getting back late.

8
00:00:34.459 --> 00:00:38.890
Why don't you stay with the Harpers tonight, near the landing."

9
00:00:38.891 --> 00:00:41.767
When Tom heard this, he hatched a plan.

10
00:00:41.768 --> 00:00:47.338
"Becky," he said, "let's spend the night at Widow Douglas' house instead.

11
00:00:47.339 --> 00:00:49.236
She'll have ice cream."

12
00:00:49.237 --> 00:00:53.713
Becky was about to say no when Tom reminded her that her mother would never know.

13
00:00:53.714 --> 00:00:55.395
So she agreed.

14
00:00:55.396 --> 00:01:01.415
The ferry dropped the picnickers off at a spot about three miles from town.

15
00:01:01.416 --> 00:01:07.396
After they had eaten and played some games, somebody yelled, "Who's ready for the cave?"

16
00:01:07.397 --> 00:01:13.926
Everyone shouted, "Yay!" So candles were quickly provided, and the children entered the cave.

17
00:01:13.927 --> 00:01:20.592
The cave was a confusing maze of twisting and turning tunnels, but most of the boys knew their way around a lot of it.

18
00:01:20.593 --> 00:01:24.626
After a while the boys and girls returned to the cave entrance.

19
00:01:24.627 --> 00:01:29.842
Soon the ferry blew its whistle. Night was falling, and it was time to go.

20
00:01:29.843 --> 00:01:34.686
The picnickers boarded the boat and amused themselves with tales of their adventures.

21
00:01:34.687 --> 00:01:39.754
No one noticed that Tom and Becky were missing.

22
00:01:39.755 --> 00:01:42.508
Meanwhile Huck was watching the tavern.

23
00:01:42.509 --> 00:01:47.635
Huck was hiding deep in the shadows when he saw two men leave by the alley door.

24
00:01:47.636 --> 00:01:52.287
To Huck's surprise, one of the men seemed to be carrying a box under his arm.

25
00:01:52.288 --> 00:01:59.879
Huck was determined not to let the treasure escape him twice, so he followed the men.

26
00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.123
They headed toward the ferry landing, and then a little out of town.

27
00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:07.651
They stopped near the Widow Douglas' house.

28
00:02:07.652 --> 00:02:12.005
"There are lights on," growled Injun Joe. "She must have company."

29
00:02:12.006 --> 00:02:15.524
"Maybe we shouldn't do this," said the second man.

30
00:02:15.525 --> 00:02:19.883
"No way," said Injun Joe. "I want revenge.

31
00:02:19.884 --> 00:02:23.526
Her husband horsewhipped me, but he died before I could—"

32
00:02:23.527 --> 00:02:26.734
"Are you going to kill her?" interrupted the other man.

33
00:02:26.735 --> 00:02:28.912
"I won't do any killing."

34
00:02:28.913 --> 00:02:32.665
"Kill? Who said kill?" answered Injun Joe.

35
00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:36.564
Huck had heard enough. He turned and slowly moved away.

36
00:02:36.565 --> 00:02:41.146
Once he was sure that he couldn't be heard or seen, he ran.

37
00:02:41.147 --> 00:02:43.976
Huck stopped at the first house he came to.

38
00:02:43.977 --> 00:02:47.166
It was the Welshman's house, and he banged on the door.

39
00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:52.733
As soon as the Welshman opened the door, Huck told him that Widow Douglas might be in danger.

40
00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:56.859
The Welshman and his sons grabbed their guns and ran into the night.

41
00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:01.331
Huck returned at dawn to learn what had happened.

42
00:03:01.332 --> 00:03:04.638
"Sit down, boy," said the Welshman.

43
00:03:04.639 --> 00:03:08.067
"First we'll have breakfast, and then we'll trade stories."

44
00:03:08.068 --> 00:03:15.348
After breakfast Huck learned that Injun Joe and his partner had gotten away, but that the box contained only thieves' tools.

45
00:03:15.349 --> 00:03:18.132
Huck told the Welshman almost everything he knew.

46
00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:23.382
The Welshman was shocked that he and his boys had almost captured Injun Joe.

47
00:03:23.383 --> 00:03:28.809
All through the morning Huck stayed out of sight because he didn't want anyone to know that he was involved.

48
00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:33.610
The Welshman had a lot of visitors who wanted to hear the tale, and he told them.

49
00:03:33.611 --> 00:03:40.243
But he never mentioned Huck's name; instead he described a mystery man who had warned him of the crime.

50
00:03:40.244 --> 00:03:45.151
Soon the town was as curious about the mystery man as they were about the crime.

51
00:03:45.152 --> 00:03:48.413
But the Welshman wouldn't reveal Huck's identity.

52
00:03:48.414 --> 00:03:54.745
Although there was no Sunday school during summer vacation, the whole town gathered at the church.

53
00:03:54.746 --> 00:03:59.461
People wanted to hear more news about the thieves and the mystery man.

54
00:03:59.462 --> 00:04:04.807
Before long a new mystery appeared: where were Becky Thatcher and Tom Sawyer?

55
00:04:04.808 --> 00:04:06.639
No one knew.

56
00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.633
Judge Thatcher organized a search party, and the group went to the cave.

57
00:04:10.634 --> 00:04:15.695
They looked for Becky and Tom for three straight days, but were unable to find them.

58
00:04:15.696 --> 00:04:22.010
The only thing they found was Tom and Becky's names written on the wall of the cave.

59
00:04:22.011 --> 00:04:28.601
While Huck was following the thieves and most of the town was sleeping, Tom and Becky had become lost in the cave.

60
00:04:28.602 --> 00:04:34.769
Tom was an experienced explorer, but while he was with Becky, he had forgotten to mark their path.

61
00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:38.338
When he realized they were lost, it was too late.

62
00:04:38.339 --> 00:04:45.704
Becky cried, and Tom did his best to comfort her.

